310	    /**
311	     * Move a claim to a new status, recording the event; refused (and nothing written) when the
312	     * claim's current status does not allow the move. Settling fixes the claim's due at the rate
313	     * the person's grade has in force on the claim's date, or at the figure a statement bound it to,
314	     * with the late charge it has then frozen in.
315	     * Opening numbers the claim and records who opened it; a voided claim keeps its number, which
316	     * is never reused. The user who opened a claim,
317	     * or last edited it, is refused when settling it. A clerk settling a claim whose due is above the sheet's clerk limit
318	     * (a due of n/a is within any limit) sends it PENDING instead, for a steward to approve or reject;
319	     * a steward settles any. A move the sheet's permission matrix does not allow the user's role is
320	     * refused. A claim due by inside a closed period cannot be moved, nor can a claim
321	     * deferred on the sheet's today be settled, nor a claim opened by anyone but a steward whose person is
322	     * flagged on the sheet's today, nor a claim opened whose person already has as many OPEN
323	     * or PENDING claims due by in its period as the period's claim cap. A claim opened whose due is above the
324	     * sheet's review threshold in force on its date (a due of n/a is within any threshold) goes to REVIEW
325	     * instead, with no number yet, audited as CLAIM_REVIEW (see {@link #review}). A SETTLED claim is voided only by a steward, within
326	     * {@link ClaimStatus#VOID_SETTLED_DAYS} days of its settlement; its frozen figure leaves every
327	     * total and the audit records it as reversed.
328	     */
